  "id": "retest-reliability",
  "term": "retest reliability",
  "definition": "Retest reliability is the extent to which a measure gives similar results when the same thing is assessed again in a later session. In this context, it refers to how consistently brain connectivity measures are reproduced across two testing sessions.",
